    h_R(arcsec) x D/206.265 vs h_R(kpc): median 0.9970, max |dev| 0.0347   -> the same quantity

1b  caveat 3 -- h_z is INFERRED from h_R, not measured
    r(log h_R, log h_z) = 0.99927, slope 0.645
    h_z carries no independent information.  Unlike the scale-length
    test it does NOT cancel from the amplitude -- sigma_z^2 is linear in
    h_z -- so it is marginalised with a per-galaxy width AND a
    common-mode zero-point width, never fixed.

1c  ENDOGENEITY -- the DiskMass rotation amplitude is TF-derived
    V_c,sin i/sin(i_TF) vs V_flat(TF): max |dev| 0.0041 over 28
    The same number to rounding: the inclination came from inverting the
    K-band Tully-Fisher relation, so the deprojected circular speed IS
    the TF prediction from M_K.  Consequences, applied throughout:
      * no law is fitted to DiskMass rotation; the fits are SPARC-only;
      * the rotation-curve SHAPE (arctan r_s, hence dlnV/dlnR and the
        epicyclic sigma_theta/sigma_R) is a real measurement and IS used;
      * the Upsilon-free A_dyn of step 6c is reported TF-conditional.

1d  photometry cross-check: two independent routes to the disk light
