    alpha_eff implied by (sigma_LOS_0, sigma_z_0, i): n=28  median 0.561  16-84% [0.462, 0.605]
    Consistent with the alpha ~ 0.6 DiskMass adopt.  The forward model
    therefore predicts sigma_z, projects with ITS OWN alpha, and compares
    to sigma_LOS_0 -- the raw observable -- so the ellipsoid shape is an
    explicit nuisance rather than an inherited one.

1f  dynamic range for a DIFFERENTIAL test: mu0_K_i spans 16.03..19.89 mag/arcsec^2
    = factor 35 in central surface density; that is what a differential test can exploit.

